<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">16062026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>The United Nations has documented one thousand civilian deaths from drone strikes in Sudan in just five months.</s> <s>Armed drones have spread across the country's three-year civil war, with strikes landing on markets, homes, and shelters far from any front line.</s> <s>The UN's human rights chief, Volker Turk, warned that autonomous weapons are reshaping this war faster than any law can follow.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Israeli forces have demolished sixteen Syrian homes in the village of Al-Hamidiya, in Quneitra, months after the families were forced out.</s> <s>Israel has occupied southwest Syria since December of twenty twenty-four, razing one hundred ten acres of ancient forest, while UN figures count two hundred fifty Syrians arrested.</s> <s>Fifty of them remain detained inside Israel... and the new bases rising on their land suggest this displacement was always meant to be permanent.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A judge in Abuja has ordered five opposition parties struck from Nigeria's ballot.</s> <s>The constitution bars any party that fails to win a single seat or a quarter of the vote, and the ruling disqualifies Atiku Abubakar of the African Democratic Congress from the twenty twenty-seven race.</s> <s>The judge acted even though an appeals court had pointed the other way, leaving Nigeria's largest opposition figure suddenly without a vehicle.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Cairo, Egyptian security forces fired birdshot at residents of Warraq island, striking two children.</s> <s>The people there have spent years resisting forced displacement for a state redevelopment plan on their stretch of the Nile.</s> <s>They now face arrest campaigns and ferry blockades as the authorities tighten the seizure of their land.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Britain's Court of Appeal has upheld a ruling that places the protest group Palestine Action in the same legal category as the Islamic State.</s> <s>Outside the court, police arrested fifty-eight supporters simply for holding signs, and membership now carries years in prison.</s> <s>Co-founder Huda Ammori will seek a Supreme Court appeal, testing how far a democracy can stretch its terrorism laws around dissent.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Venezuela, the founder of the Tren de Aragua gang, known as Niño Guerrero, was killed in a joint American and Venezuelan strike.</s> <s>His network grew from a single prison into a web of autonomous cells across the hemisphere, which analysts say makes it strangely resilient to losing a leader.</s> <s>No successor has been named, and it's far from clear the strike weakens a structure built to survive exactly this.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's next federal budget sets aside eight trillion rupees just to pay interest on its debt.</s> <s>That single line now consumes nearly forty-three percent of all federal spending, after the country's debt doubled to ninety-seven trillion rupees in only four years.</s> <s>Senator Sherry Rehman warned that this leaves almost nothing for schools, hospitals, or the development the country desperately needs.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Korea has discovered just how tightly China's hand rests on its supply chains, depending on Beijing for up to ninety-four percent of some critical minerals.</s> <s>The chokepoint isn't the mines themselves but the refining, where China processes the world's ore into usable metal.</s> <s>Seoul has trimmed its dependence at the margins, yet on its most strategic minerals the grip has barely loosened.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Turkey has announced it will mobilize ten billion dollars to build its own artificial intelligence capacity.</s> <s>The plan deliberately targets domestic computing power rather than renting it from American or Chinese providers, a bid for technological sovereignty.</s> <s>The fine print, though, is missing... no funding breakdown, no procurement plan, and no timeline yet for when any of it arrives.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>NASA says sixteen cracks in a Russian tunnel module threatened the International Space Station with catastrophic failure.</s> <s>Russia approached the cracking section with a saw and shared no safety analysis, prompting five astronauts to shelter in a docked Crew Dragon capsule early this month.</s> <s>Moscow will now decommission the module entirely, removing one of the oldest and most fragile pieces of the orbiting station.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>How many fundamental particles make up the universe? Physicists meeting near Geneva can't agree, offering answers from seventeen to nearly a thousand.</s> <s>The count depends on whether you tally color charge, antiparticles, and spin states separately, which means the famous seventeen is a convention, not a fact of nature.</s> <s>Beneath the arithmetic lies a deeper unease about what physicists even mean when they call something fundamental.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Africa has approved nearly four thousand nine hundred megawatts of clean power that simply cannot reach the grid.</s> <s>The national utility, Eskom, found its transmission lines already exhausted in the three sunniest and windiest regions, the very places the new projects were meant to sit.</s> <s>Developers are now retreating to other provinces, while approved electricity waits, stranded, for wires that don't exist.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Tesla, it turns out, measured its Full Self-Driving software against airbag-triggering crashes, not against all collisions, when it made its safety case.</s> <s>The Netherlands approved the system in April after independent road tests, and Tesla is now pitching Sweden using those same disputed numbers.</s> <s>European member states vote soon on bloc-wide approval, with the meaning of the word safe quietly hanging on the fine print.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In California, a man named Casey Harrell, silenced by motor neurone disease, now reads aloud to his daughter through electrodes implanted in his brain.</s> <s>Over twenty-two months and thirty-eight hundred hours of use, the system reached ninety-seven and a half percent accuracy, researchers reported in Nature Medicine.</s> <s>The team's next goal is to restore not just his words, but the sound of his own voice.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>China is making a very different bet on artificial intelligence, releasing its most powerful models free and open for anyone in the world to use.</s> <s>The strategy aims to win over developers and erode the advantage of closed American labs like OpenAI and Anthropic.</s> <s>Whichever country's model becomes the default that the world builds upon may shape the next decade of computing.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>